{"type":"text","timestamp":1793647851420,"sessionID":"ses_e62421120ffesUfGSkpB49C3VX","part":{"id":"prt_19dbe2b1f0017y6ouxGbFHMD6Y_text-0","sessionID":"ses_e62421120ffesUfGSkpB49C3VX","messageID":"msg_19dbe2b1f0017y6ouxGbFHMD6Y","type":"text","text":"\n\n[goal] Make all three harness configs report fast-coder context window 262144, permanently, without touching any other setting.\n\n[action] The README says `out/` is generated from `models.json` by `gen.py`, so the disagreement was a symptom: `models.json` (the source of truth) said 131072, and `out/opencode.json` had drifted to 262144 by a hand edit that the next `python gen.py` would have wiped. I edited only `models.json` line 3 (`131072` → `262144`) and reran `python gen.py` to regenerate all three files. Assumption: fixing the source and regenerating is what \"for good\" means; hand-editing `out/` would be overwritten on the next generation.\n\n[result] Regeneration printed `wrote out/opencode.json / codex.toml / claude.json`. A `Compare-Object` diff of `out/` before vs after shows exactly two changes: `context_window = 131072` → `262144` in `out/codex.toml` and `\"contextWindow\": 131072` → `262144` in `out/claude.json`; `out/opencode.json` diffed empty (its hand-edited value now matches the generator). A grep for `131072|262144` across the repo finds 262144 in all four files and zero occurrences of 131072. All other values (max_output, tool_calling, deep-thinker, tiny-chat) are byte-identical per the diff.\n\n[next] Nothing required; if these files are under version control, commit the two-file change (`models.json` plus regenerated `out/`).","time":{"start":1793647848241,"end":1793647851420}}}

